}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2a1713-45a0-5ac9-812e-efe047dbc9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector in a New Basis Given the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1716bdc6-24bd-510f-89d5-ab35a3bdb21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440401} {:answer/id #uuid "182873b5-14af-5685-85b8-f194b83b4644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440403} {:answer/id #uuid "4741e426-3e99-5468-9275-81e55bc048d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440416} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e4e105-32ed-5a4b-aa6e-4d1ffb7d3512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440444} {:answer/id #uuid "d88d77fd-b7e5-5e52-b6d5-70171e5b3e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440446}] :answer-field/c